- What optimizations reduce time to O(n^2) or enable pruning of the i-loop?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests a novel fixed-gap non-crossing pairing constraint, a natural extension of classic non-crossing matching problems, while probing DP state design and reconstruction.

## Key Concepts
- DP over prefixes with fixed pair distance
- Non-crossing/disjoint constraint handling
- Backpointers for reconstruction
- Space/time optimization trade-offs

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxFixedGapPairs(A, d, k) {
  const n = A.length;
  const dp = Array.from({ length: n + 1 }, () => Array(k + 1).fill(-Infinity));
  const take = Array.from({ length: n + 1 }, () => Array(k + 1).fill(false));
  dp[0][0] = 0;
  for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
    for (let t = 0; t <= k; t++) {
      dp[i][t] = dp[i - 1][t];
      if (t > 0 && i - d - 1 >= 0) {
        const cand = dp[i - d - 1][t - 1] + A[i - 1] * A[i - d - 1];
        if (cand > dp[i][t]) {
          dp[i][t] = cand;
          take[i][t] = true;
        }
      }
    }
  }
  const pairs = [];
  let i = n, t = k;
  while (t > 0 && i > 0) {
    if (take[i][t]) {
      pairs.push([i - d, i]); // 1-based indices of the pair
      i = i - d - 1;
      t--;
    } else {
      i--;
    }
  }
  pairs.reverse();
  return { value: dp[n][k], pairs };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests a new DP variant: maximizing the sum of non-additive subarray values (bitwise OR) while enforcing exactly k non-overlapping blocks. It also probes reconstruction logic for end-to-start blocks.

## Key Concepts
- DP over partitioning into k non-overlapping blocks
- Non-additive block value via OR, requiring on-the-fly accumulation
- Backpointers for exact block endpoints

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxKOrSubarrays(A, k){
  const n=A.length;
  const dp=Array.from({length:n+1}, ()=> Array(k+1).fill(-Infinity));
  const prv=Array.from({length:n+1}, ()=> Array(k+1).fill(-1));
  dp[0][0]=0;
  for(let i=0;i<n;i++){
    for(let t=1;t<=k;t++){
      let curr=0;
      for(let j=i;j>=0;j--){
        curr |= A[j];
        let left = dp[j][t-1];
        if(left>-Infinity){
          const cand = left + curr;
          if(cand>dp[i+1][t]){ dp[i+1][t]=cand; prv[i+1][t]=j; }
        }
      }
    }
  }
  return {value: dp[n][k], endAt: prv};
}
```

